content.text:
I found clear evidence. Candidate_01 ("Move pending objects (orgs, users) into a dedicated branch") introduces the exact bug: in `NewAccountFormController.java`, it adds the code block:
```java
if(account.getOrg().length() > 0) {
    Org org = orgDao.findByCommonName(account.getOrg());
    orgDao.addUser(org, account);
}
```
This is precisely the call referenced in the fix commit message. Moreover, this same commit rewrote `NewAccountFormControllerTest.java` introducing the `mockAccountDao`/`mockOrgDao` field names and `configureFormBean()` setting `formBean.getOrg()` to `"geOrchestra testing team"` — but never stubbed `mockOrgDao.findByCommonName(...)`. The fix commit's diff builds directly on top of this exact structure (same variable names `mockAccountDao`, `mockOrgDao`, and org name `"geOrchestra testing team"`), adding the missing `when(mockOrgDao.findByCommonName(eq(orgName))).thenReturn(mockOrg);` stub. Candidate_02 is a large pure code-formatting commit unrelated to this logic.

