The fix commit message states: "Fixes NewAccountFormControllerTest, the call to orgDao.findByCommonName(...) in NewAccountFormController is not mocked up and resulted in NPE." The fix diff adds a mock for `mockOrgDao.findByCommonName(eq(orgName))` in `NewAccountFormControllerTest.java`, using variables named `mockAccountDao`, `mockOrgDao`, and an org name constant `"geOrchestra testing team"`.

Candidate_01 ("Move pending objects (orgs, users) into a dedicated branch") is the commit that introduces this exact call in `console/src/main/java/org/georchestra/console/ws/newaccount/NewAccountFormController.java`:

```java
String requestOriginator = request.getHeader("sec-username");
accountDao.insert(account, requestOriginator);
roleDao.addUser(Role.USER, account, requestOriginator);
if(account.getOrg().length() > 0) {
    Org org = orgDao.findByCommonName(account.getOrg());
    orgDao.addUser(org, account);
}
```

This same commit also rewrote `NewAccountFormControllerTest.java`, introducing the exact field names later referenced by the fix (`mockAccountDao`, `mockOrgDao`), and a `configureFormBean()` helper that stubs `formBean.getOrg()` to return `"geOrchestra testing team"` (a non-empty value), which triggers the new `orgDao.findByCommonName(...)` code path during the `create()` test flow — but the commit never added a corresponding stub for `mockOrgDao.findByCommonName(...)`. The fix commit's diff is a minimal, direct patch on top of exactly this test structure, confirming candidate_01 as the bug-introducing commit.

Candidate_02 ("Re-apply code formatting with proper settings") is a large, purely mechanical whitespace/formatting refactor across the whole codebase using maven-formatter-plugin, with no functional/logic changes, and is unrelated to the introduction of the `findByCommonName` call or the org/pending-account feature.

